There are different types of tape. Roughly speaking, you can choose between traditional tape and athletic tape.
Traditional tape is used to hold muscles or bones in a certain position. This is mainly used near joints, such as ankles, wrists and hands.
In addition, some players just like the idea that their cleats are more secure and less likely to come loose during a match.
Ideally, you should use stretch tape for taping your ankles.
However, don't forget to check your league's rules beforehand to make sure splashing is allowed.
By compressing the muscle, traditional athletic tape can help reduce swelling, which can relieve pain and prevent further injury.
In many cases, athletes also use less restrictive tape to help prevent injuries.
The importance of this tape is that it is used during exercise to lightly lift the skin, leaving enough space between the skin and the muscles to promote blood flow and lymphatic drainage.
It naturally returns to its original position, which takes some of the workload off the muscle.
In addition, it can correct posture problems that may be the result of an injury or pre-existing condition.
The tape has become something of a trend. Consider, for example, Alvin Kamara, who wears a long strip of tape across the entire back of his arm.
Prevention is the main reason football athletes tap their fingers, but in practice it can also help players recover from injuries faster than usual.
