More information Investing in a good facemask will make a big difference during competitions and training.
The facemask, which is attached to your helmet, is the only barrier between your face and your opponent. And that's really just a thin piece of metal.
You can read more about this in this article.
With this article I want to help you find the right facemask for your situation through detailed buying instructions.
Not only do you have a durable and strong product with this facemask, it is also very affordable and can be used by players of different positions. Assembly is easy and comes with the required fasteners.
View the table below and read on for more information about each facemask, and how to choose the best facemask.
Best American Football facemask for all positions & made of carbon steel: Xenith Prime
You don't just buy a facemask. There are some things you should know before buying a facemask for your American Football helmet.
The only drawback compared to the other two materials is that it is much heavier. Carbon steel facemasks are often chosen by aspiring football athletes and youth players.
Stainless steel facemasks are the perfect combination of light weight and robustness. They are lighter than carbon steel facemasks, but also slightly more expensive.
This type of material is often recommended for the more serious youth and high school athletes, as well as for the 'casual' adult player.
Titanium is the preferred choice of professionals, college athletes and elite high school athletes. The material is light in weight, but at the same time strong and durable.
Titanium is 60% lighter than the traditional carbon steel facemask and much stronger than steel. The titanium facemasks are also the most expensive on the market.
One of the most important purposes of a facemask is of course protection. Your goal should be to get a sturdy, durable and protective facemask.
In addition, you can also base your choice on the way you would like to express yourself and distinguish yourself from the rest. For example, choose one with cool patterns and colors.
Facemasks are designed to protect the face, especially the eyes, nose and mouth. When choosing a facemask, both your face must be protected and the field of view must remain clear.
A facemask with many transverse bars higher up over the eyes will protect the player, but it will also obstruct the view.
On the other hand, a more open bar configuration would provide more visibility, but would be less protective of the mouth and eyes from the opponent's fingers or hands.
Players involved in blocking, tackling or other forms of hard contact are advised to wear a closed face mask.
In addition, a closed facemask gives extra support to the jawline to prevent damage to the teeth and mouth.
They are suitable for defensive linemen who want maximum protection for the mouth, eyes, face and chin. A closed mask is also suitable for offensive linemen, fullbacks and linebackers.
