Although all kinds of stone surface repair technology is constantly born, the effect after repair is still very difficult to be completely consistent with the natural appearance of stone itself. As for the color difference, grain size, the uniformity and consistency of surface color spots and flower spots, which can not be changed by human beings, why should we blame the whole when using natural stone materials and ask them to be perfect?
Crack: a small crack in rock. It can be divided into open fracture and dark crack.
Dark crack refers to those cracks that are not obvious, and it is difficult to distinguish the crack line from the outer surface of the stone block before processing, and the crack line extends short.
Stone cracks are commonly found in those Beige stone (such as old beige, saanna beige, Spanish Beige) and white stones such as Dahua white and Yashi white. Purplish red and brown reticulation are also common.
When it comes to the problem of cracks in natural stone materials, I think of the case of a well-known domestic real estate enterprise processing Shaana Beige products at the end of the last century
In the face of such strict quality requirements of the project, the company boss communicated with the project inspection personnel and said that “the Shaanna beige is full of cracks, and those without cracks are not Shaanna beige.”
