Does God raise himself up as a servant?
Did God highly exalt Christ and give him the name that is above every name because he was obedient to himself?
A high priest works on behalf of God in relation to men, so how is it that God designated himself a high priest?
If Jesus already is God and all things are subjected to God, does it make any sense to say “God has put all things in subjection under his feet”?
If Christ is God, how can it be said that Christ has entered “into heaven itself, now to appear in the presence of God on our behalf”?
Why does Jesus say numerous times he is going to the Father if he is the Father?
How can God be tempted in every way we are and also sympathize with our weaknesses?
Jesus was taught by God. Does God need to learn anything?
If Jesus, is God, he would have the Holy Spirit within himself. So rather from descending from heaven and reside with him, wouldn’t it rather emanate from him?
If Jesus is himself God, why would an angel be needed to strengthen him?
God has no need to anoint himself. Why would Jesus need to be anointed by God with the Holy Spirit?
Why does Jesus have no glory in himself if he is God?
If Jesus himself is the Father, what sense does it make to say that the Father loves Jesus because he lays down his life?
Jesus said that Father is greater than all. Why not just say that he is Greater than all?
Why does Jesus refer to the Father as the only true God and as himself as the one that he had sent?
Why does Jesus refer to God as His God and his Father if he himself is the Father?
Why is the Father referred to the one God and source of all things while Jesus referred to as the the one Lord (as a distinction between him and God) in 1 Cor 8:5-6?
In distinction to God, Jesus is referred as a man who is the one mediator between God and men in 1 Tim 2:5-6. How can God be both the mediator and the God he mediates for?
