Four key points for cat food purchase
Cats have a high demand for protein. It is best to choose cat food in the range of 36% to 48%, and only animal protein has a high absorption rate and vegetable protein is very low.
Cats cannot synthesize by themselves and can only rely on eating. Therefore, cat food with taurine ≥ 0.1% should be selected at a minimum, and 0.2% or more is the best when conditions permit.
The calcium-to-phosphorus ratio of cat food is recommended to be kept in the range of 1.1:1~1.4:1. The ratio is unbalanced, which can easily lead to abnormal bone development of cats.
Most of the cat food with the public proportion is good cat food. I don’t dare to say absolutely, but I dare to disclose it, which proves that I have confidence in the product and are willing to accept supervision.
Everyone knows that you get what you pay for. If you buy a cat food for a few dollars a pound, it will claim to be high-protein cat food, which is not credible.
But cat food is not the more expensive the better, the right one is the best.
First, see if the cat food is too greasy to the touch. If it is too greasy, don’t choose it, because long-term consumption will cause problems such as cat anger, soft stools, and black chin.
Finally, taste whether it is too salty. If it is too salty, it means that the salt content is high, and long-term consumption will cause tears and hair loss in cats.
