How to distinguish which kind of dog food is good for natural dog food
Commercial food refers to pet food made from 4D raw materials (there may be by-products such as fur, unsafe factors such as sick and dead poultry), and usually add food attractants (taste enhancers), which most cats and dogs love to eat. There are also additions of antioxidants such as BHT, preservatives, stool coagulants, etc.
What is natural dog food From the American AAFCO’s definition of natural grains: feed or ingredients derived entirely from plants, animals or minerals, material untreated, or physically treated, heat-treated, defatted, purified, extracted, hydrolyzed, enzymatically hydrolyzed or fermented, but not Made by or by chemical synthesis, without any chemically synthesized additives or processing aids, except for the unavoidable circumstances that may occur in good manufacturing practice.
In terms of ingredients, all natural grains come from fresh ingredients, and there is evidence to check where the ingredients are sourced. Long-term use, the dog’s hair and poop are healthier.
At present, many dog food brands on the domestic market have launched natural food.
In theory, there are few natural ingredients in the domestic dog food on the market. It is only the difference between the quality of the raw materials, but it does not mean that this kind of dog food No, in fact, there is no need to blindly believe in natural food, some domestic big brands of dog food are also very good!
The 4D component is the abbreviation of the animals in the following four states: Dead, Diseased, Dying, and Disabled, and by-products refer to their internal organs, fur, etc. Although the material of commercial food is not attractive to dogs, by adding a lot of food attractants, it is generally more fragrant, and most dogs love to eat it.
If it is particularly fragrant, this kind of dog food must not be natural food, but a lot of food attractants have been added in it. The aroma of natural dog food is not strong, but it will be lighter, and the surface may not be regular enough, and the shoddy dog food is particularly regular.
I believe that there are too many benefits of natural grains, but everyone is most concerned about the price issue. It is true that natural grains do not have an advantage in terms of price, because the current sales channels of natural grains are mainly imported.
Disadvantage 2 of natural food: the palatability of dogs is slightly lower
Since there are no food attractants added in natural food, dogs may not like to eat it when they first come into contact with them, and the palatability is obviously not as good as commercial food, but as long as dogs insist on eating, they will find that natural food made of fresh materials It can greatly improve the dog’s appetite, and the initial not eating is just an excess. How to identify natural dog food?
Natural dog food must be free of hormones, attractants, preservatives, antibiotics, artificial colors, and chemical additives. From raw materials, processing, to finished products, it is a chemical-free dog food produced by a natural production system.
