Additionally, Geeks in Cambodia sat down with Ms Botum Rangsay, the Secretary of State for the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, in order to provide you with the latest insights on CICTA.
Seeing how important this competition is in promoting the ICT sector, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications decided to make CICTA happen. The CICTA program will provide ICT sectors in Cambodia with many opportunities.
What do you think the digital trends (Internet, Mobile…) for Cambodia could be like in the future? For example, based on the latest numbers that we have featured on our Digital Trends in Cambodia article, how do you foresee the evolution?
So, what are you waiting for?
With the digital sector increasingly growing in the Kingdom, CICTA aspires to heighten understanding in the ICT industry, as well as aid in bringing the digital gap between business communities and people in the cities / provinces closer.
Held at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications in Phnom Penh, CICTA has several categories of awards, which includes:
Private Sector: made up of private sector related ICT products (Industrial Application, e-Logistics, Supply Chain Management, etc.)
Digital Content: made up of ICT products that are linked to the practice of connecting text, sound, pictures, and videos, to create multimedia, infotainment, immersion, and interaction for the community
Research and Development: made up of ICT products that are freshly being researched and made
5th June – Shortlist Announcement
