We all know that over the years, mankind has harnessed the power of technology to improve lives all over the world. Many new inventions have come about as a result of technology, bringing along with them increased convenience to our daily activities.
In this month’s edition, we bring you 4 different wacky gadgets for you to decide if they are insane, or genius. So sit back, and have fun with this crazy list!
The smart tumblr instantly displays the nutritional contents of the beverage you pour in as well, which in turn gets synced into your smartphone so that you can track your drinking habits.
The cup can be considered genius, because Vessyl is the first of its kind to make use of molecular sensors to record every drink that you intake, making it a truly innovative invention. However, the catch is that the smart cup costs USD$99.
For USD$99, this 3D printer promises to let you print anything out of chocolate. Sounds magical enough for you?
Fret not, for the Lock N Load Gun Alarm Clock is sure to solve that problem for you. With a red target on the alarm clock that sprints up as soon as the alarm goes off, one has to take the gun that comes along with it and fire at the centre to shut it off.
And if that still doesn’t get you out of bed, get this – the alarm clock has several game modes, including “quick shot”, where you will have to score five perfect shots in a period of 3 minutes! How wacky is that?
So what did you think?
Let us know in the comments below!
The hands on workshop focused on several topics like crowd-advocacy, cloud connection, and open paradigm participation. The Mekong ICT Camp featured workshops and panel discussions, which helped attendees garner more information about open source technologies, as well as understand concepts so as to come up with and design project challenges.
