From the inspiration behind WildScan to its impacts on Cambodia’s wildlife, we spoke to Matthew Prichett, Deputy Director of Communications at Freeland, and Amy Van Nice, Deputy Director of Programs at Wildlife Alliance, to find out more.
How did the idea for the app come about?
Apart from identifying endangered animals, how else does the app help to stop illegal wildlife trade?
How will this app impact Cambodia and its wildlife?
As this app would require the participation of Cambodians, are there efforts in promoting the app? If so, what has been done so far?
What do you hope to achieve with this app?
It is a five year program designed to combat wildlife trafficking in Southeast Asia and China). WildScan can play an important role in Cambodia to this effect and we are grateful for our partner and longtime friend, Freeland, for taking the initiative and putting in many years of hard work to bring this useful tool to fruition.
